RimCourt.Court.PetitionDef.caseText:
{OTHER_labelShort} broke, picked {PETITIONER_labelShort} out, and came to kill {PETITIONER_objective}. It did not work, which is the only reason {PETITIONER_labelShort} can stand here and say so.{REPEAT}

{OTHER_labelShort} says {OTHER_pronoun} was not in {OTHER_possessive} right mind. {PETITIONER_labelShort} says it felt real enough.

How does the lord rule?

{OTHER_labelShort} broke, went to the graves, and dug up {DETAIL}. Then {OTHER_pronoun} carried the body back among the living and left it where everyone would find it.{REPEAT}

{PETITIONER_labelShort} wants the lord to say what is owed to the dead.

How does the lord rule?

{OTHER_labelShort} broke, and went round the colony setting fires. {OTHER_pronoun} put a flame to {DETAIL}.{REPEAT}

{PETITIONER_labelShort} has brought it before the lord. {OTHER_labelShort} says it was the breakdown and not {OTHER_objective}. Both can be true.

How does the lord rule?

{OTHER_labelShort} broke, went down to the cells, and tried to talk {DETAIL} into breaking out. Whatever came of it, {OTHER_pronoun} worked to open a door the colony keeps shut.{REPEAT}

{PETITIONER_labelShort} has brought it before the lord.

How does the lord rule?

{OTHER_labelShort} broke, and went among the colony's animals with a knife. {OTHER_pronoun} killed {DETAIL}.{REPEAT}

{PETITIONER_labelShort} wants the lord to say what that cost the colony. {OTHER_labelShort} would rather it was not counted.

How does the lord rule?

{OTHER_labelShort} went into a rage and took it out on {DETAIL}.{REPEAT}

{PETITIONER_labelShort} wants it answered for. {OTHER_labelShort} says the colony pushed {OTHER_objective} to it.

How does the lord rule?
